## Variant: :quick
- Run ONLY Phase 1 (signal scanner, 3 WebSearches)
- Generate 3 questions (not 5-7)
- Apply only core lenses (no conditionals)
- Output: 20-30 lines short verdict
- Skip analysis history save (too shallow to track)

## Variant: :deep
- Force Tier 3 deep dive regardless of Phase 1 signals
- Generate 7 questions (max)
- Activate ALL conditional agents that could be relevant
- Apply 9 lenses (all core + most relevant conditionals)
- Output: 120-180 lines (allow longer for depth)
- Save to analysis history

## Variant: :resume {slug}
- Load previous analysis from data/analysis-history/{slug}.json
- Restore `intent_meta` including `prompt_intelligence` from saved state
  - If saved state lacks `prompt_intelligence` (pre-V17): re-extract from `intent_meta.original_query`
  - If `original_query` also missing: proceed without (graceful degradation)
- Pass restored `prompt_intelligence` to all re-run agents via context injection
- Display questions, verdict, predictions
- Ask user: "What's changed since {date}?"
- Re-run only the questions affected by changes
- Update analysis history file (append, don't overwrite)
- Save as new version: {date}-{slug}-v2.json

